      "number": 4,
      "paragraphs": [
        "1: dot products",
        "Example",
        "A : [1 2]",
        "B : [5; 7]",
        "C = 1·5 + 2·7 = 19",
        "shop 2: 3·5 + 4·7 = 43",
        "Each entry of C = AB is a dot product:",
        "c_ij = (row i of A) · (col j of B)",
        "the number of columns in the first matrix (A) must be equal to the number of rows in the second matrix (B)",
        "A: m × n",
        "B: n × p",
        "C: m × p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "paragraphs": [
        "2 and 3: columns and rows",
        "Each column of C is A times the matching column of B, so it is a linear combination of the columns of A. ",
        "Each row of C is the matching row of A times B, a linear combination of the rows of B.",
        "C = 5·[1;3] + 7·[2;4]",
        "= [19; 43]",
        "C = 1·[5 6] + 2·[7 8]",
        "= [19 22]",
        "Example",
        "C = 5·[1;3] + 7·[2;4]",
        "= [19; 43]",
        "C = 1·[5 6] + 2·[7 8]",
        "= [19 22]"
      ]
